 H1 2026 backlog was C$5.1B, about 1.21 times the guidance. Orders were up 11%, and cancellations were under 1%.\n- Quarterly revenue (C$M) was 905, 960, 980, then 890 in 2026Q2. That sums to about C$3.74B over the last four quarters.\n- Reaching C$4.2B needs about 12% growth on that, or roughly C$1,050M a quarter. The best quarter so far is 980.\n- The Halbrook plant was down for nine weeks and restarted in August. Management expects to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027, which is unverified.\n- The disclosures alone suggest roughly C$3.9–4.2B, with the guidance at the top of that range. Node n2 put the odds at 50–60%.\n\n**Industry data (node n3):**\n- Caldrian transformer shipments fell 4% year on year in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years.\n- Voltaris shipments fell 9%, and its market share dropped from 31% to 27%.\n- Shipments trail orders by about two quarters, so the weakness likely carries into 2027.\n- Holding the Q2 run rate gives about C$3.56B. Continued share loss gives C$3.4–3.5B. Node n3 estimated C$3.4–3.7B.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The backlog disclosure doesn't say how much converts to revenue in 2027.\n- Node n3 had only one quarter of share and shipment data.\n- Revenue may follow price and mix rather than units, which could help Voltaris.","ttft_ms":3642,"type":"result","duration_ms":40155,"uuid":"3c7237b2-f095-42fd-96a4-e4491014462a","ttft_stream_ms":2678,"time_to_request_ms":204,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":24,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":18,"init_frame_send":13,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":14,"request_announcements":28,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":47,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":7,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":154,